---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import KeyFacts from '../../components/KeyFacts.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import AuthorBox from '../../components/AuthorBox.astro';
import Sources from '../../components/Sources.astro';
import Photo from '../../components/Photo.astro';
import { site, rates } from '../../data/site';
import { tours } from '../../data/tours';
import { article } from '../../lib/schema';

const base = Astro.site!;
const path = '/guides/driver-vs-train/';
const title = 'Private driver vs train vs tuk-tuk in Sri Lanka (2026)';
const description =
  'Cost, speed, comfort and luggage compared, plus the 2026 Kandy–Ella train status: trains run Nanu Oya → Ella, but the Kandy end is still closed.';
const sedanEach = rates.sedan.perDay / 2;
// Kandy → Ella by road, taken from the 7-day itinerary so the numbers match the tour pages.
const [toNuwara, toElla] = ['Kandy → Nuwara Eliya', 'Nuwara Eliya → Ella'].map((r) => tours[0].plan.find((d) => d.route === r)!);
const roadKm = toNuwara.km + toElla.km;
const roadHours = parseFloat(toNuwara.hours) + parseFloat(toElla.hours);

const sources = [
  { title: 'Sunday Times (21 June 2026): Podi Menike runs again from Nanu Oya to Badulla', url: 'https://www.sundaytimes.lk/260621/news/podi-menike-hits-the-tracks-from-nanu-oya-to-badulla-marking-latest-phase-of-restoration-646913.html' },
  { title: 'Newswire (8 Sept 2026): Nanu Oya–Great Western railway repairs to be completed by December', url: 'https://www.newswire.lk/2026/09/08/nanu-oya-great-western-railway-repairs-to-be-completed-by-december/' },
  { title: 'The Morning (19 April 2026): Cyclone Ditwah: Upcountry rail repairs miss key targets', url: 'https://www.themorning.lk/articles/5hM6S1G0upunOodLALoX' },
  { title: 'The Common Wanderer: Kandy to Ella train guide', url: 'https://thecommonwanderer.com/blog/kandy-to-ella-train-guide' },
];
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Driver vs train vs tuk-tuk', path }]}
  schema={[article(base, { title, description, path, published: '2026-10-02', modified: site.lastUpdated })]}
>
  <h1>Private driver vs train vs tuk-tuk in Sri Lanka</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    For most trips of a week or more, a private driver is the easiest way to see Sri Lanka: US${rates.sedan.perDay} a day
    for a sedan works out at US${sedanEach} each for two people, door to door. The train is cheaper and the hill-country
    stretch is spectacular, but in 2026 it only runs from Nanu Oya to Ella. Tuk-tuks are for short trips in town.
  </p>

  <KeyFacts>
    <ul>
      <li>Private driver: US${rates.sedan.perDay} per day per sedan, US${sedanEach} per person for two, fuel and tolls included.</li>
      <li>Kandy → Ella by road: about {roadKm} km and {roadHours} hours of driving via Nuwara Eliya. By train it normally takes 6–7 hours.</li>
      <li>Since 20 June 2026 the hill-country train runs Nanu Oya → Ella → Badulla; the Kandy end of the line is still closed after Cyclone Ditwah.</li>
      <li>Tuk-tuks suit short town trips; they are not allowed on the expressways.</li>
      <li>Many travellers combine both: a driver for most days, the train for the Ella stretch.</li>
    </ul>
  </KeyFacts>

  <h2>How do a driver, the train and a tuk-tuk compare?</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="stack">
      <caption>Driver costs are {site.name} rates; train timing is for normal service on the Kandy–Ella line.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col"></th>
          <th scope="col">Private driver</th>
          <th scope="col">Train</th>
          <th scope="col">Tuk-tuk</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Cost</th>
          <td data-label="Private driver">US${rates.sedan.perDay}/day per sedan, US${rates.van.perDay}/day per van; shared by the group</td>
          <td data-label="Train">Cheapest per person</td>
          <td data-label="Tuk-tuk">Agreed per ride; cheap for short hops</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Speed</th>
          <td data-label="Private driver">Door to door; Kandy → Ella about {roadHours} h</td>
          <td data-label="Train">Slow; Kandy → Ella normally 6–7 h</td>
          <td data-label="Tuk-tuk">Slow; not allowed on expressways</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Comfort</th>
          <td data-label="Private driver">Private, air-conditioned</td>
          <td data-label="Train">Reserved seats are comfortable; unreserved carriages get crowded</td>
          <td data-label="Tuk-tuk">Open-sided, no air conditioning</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Luggage</th>
          <td data-label="Private driver">Stays in the car all trip</td>
          <td data-label="Train">You carry it on and off</td>
          <td data-label="Tuk-tuk">Small bags only</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Flexibility</th>
          <td data-label="Private driver">Stop anywhere, change the route each day</td>
          <td data-label="Train">Fixed timetable, stations only</td>
          <td data-label="Tuk-tuk">Flexible within a town</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Best for</th>
          <td data-label="Private driver">Multi-stop trips, families, groups of 2+</td>
          <td data-label="Train">The scenic hill-country stretch; solo budget travel</td>
          <td data-label="Tuk-tuk">Getting around Kandy, Ella or Galle</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Is the Kandy to Ella train running in 2026?</h2>
  <p>
    Only part of the way. Cyclone Ditwah in late November 2025 damaged the Colombo–Badulla line in 223 places. The
    section from Nanu Oya (near Nuwara Eliya) through Ella to Badulla reopened on 20 June 2026, when the Podi Menike
    started running again. The Kandy end, from Rambukkana to Nanu Oya, is still suspended: repairs between Nanu Oya and
    Great Western are targeted for December 2026, and the full line for the end of 2026. Earlier deadlines have slipped,
    so check the status shortly before you travel.
  </p>
  <p>
    What this means in practice: you cannot board at Kandy this year. Drive to Nanu Oya (or stay in Nuwara Eliya) and take
    the train from there to Ella, which is the most photographed part of the route, including the Nine Arches Bridge
    just outside Ella.
  </p>

  <Photo name="nineArches" sizes="(min-width: 760px) 720px, 100vw" />

  <blockquote>
    <p>
      “Most of my guests take the train for the Ella part. I drive their bags round and wait at the station, so they get the
      views without carrying suitcases on and off the carriage.”
    </p>
    <footer>{site.driverQuoteName}</footer>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>When is the train the better choice?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You travel alone on a tight budget: one train ticket costs far less than a day of driver hire.</li>
    <li>You want the scenic ride itself. The Nanu Oya → Ella stretch through tea estates is the reason most visitors take the train.</li>
    <li>Your route follows the railway and you travel light.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Is it worth hiring a private driver in Sri Lanka?</h2>
  <p>
    For most first-time visitors on a 7–14 day trip, yes. Sigiriya, Dambulla, Polonnaruwa, Yala and the south coast are
    not on one railway line, so a driver saves bus changes and lets you see two or three places a day. The cost falls with
    group size: US${sedanEach} each per day for two in a sedan, or about US${Math.round(rates.van.perDay / 6)} each for six in a
    van. It is less worth it if you travel solo on a budget, or stay in one or two places.
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/tours/7-day-classic/">7-day itinerary with a private driver</a> for a route that combines the car and
    the Ella train, and <a href="/pricing/">how much a private driver in Sri Lanka costs</a> for the full price breakdown.
  </p>

  <section class="related">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/pricing/">Private driver prices in Sri Lanka</a></li>
      <li><a href="/tours/10-day-highlights/">10-day Sri Lanka itinerary with a private driver</a></li>
      <li><a href="/guides/airport-transfers/">Colombo airport (CMB) transfers: times and prices</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Cta />
  <AuthorBox />
  <Sources items={sources} />
</Base>
